## Mobile track (Platform = `mobile` or `cross` on mobile files)

### Default stack
- **Component library:** [react-native-reusables](https://reactnativereusables.com) (RNR) — the mobile sibling of shadcn/ui by the same author (`@mrzachnugent`, who also merged the official Expo PR #7540 into shadcn/ui core). Same philosophy: copy-paste, NativeWind v4, class-variance-authority, radix-style primitives.
- **Framework:** Expo + React Native (SDK 52+).
- **Styling:** [NativeWind v4](https://www.nativewind.dev) (Tailwind for React Native) as default. StyleSheet API as fallback when you need raw control.
- **Navigation:** Expo Router (file-based, type-safe).
- **Animations:** React Native Reanimated 3 — never the legacy Animated API.
- **Gestures:** React Native Gesture Handler.
- **Safe-area:** `react-native-safe-area-context` (`SafeAreaView` on every screen).
- **Agent discovery / install:** shadcn MCP (when you run `npx shadcn init` in an Expo project, the CLI auto-detects and uses RNR's registry).
- **Prototyping surface:** Claude Design in mobile mode (the prompt must say "mobile app, iOS + Android, use Expo Router, NativeWind") + Expo Go for on-device preview.
- **Handoff:** Claude Code reads the prototype bundle + memory/14 + DESIGN.md + the mobile CLAUDE.md template (see `.cursor/templates/CLAUDE.md.mobile.md`).

### Non-negotiables (mobile)
1. No bespoke UI library unless `memory/14 §Installed components` and `memory/07-decisions-log.md` explain why. Default is RNR.
2. `components.json` must exist at the repo root (RNR respects shadcn's config format).
3. **Minimize `Platform.OS` branches.** Prefer a single component that adapts via props or safe-area context. If you have more than 3 `Platform.OS === 'ios'` checks in one file, refactor.
4. **Always wrap screens in `SafeAreaView`** from `react-native-safe-area-context`. No raw top/bottom padding.
5. **Use Expo Router**, not React Navigation imperatively. `router.replace('/auth/login')` instead of `navigation.navigate(...)`.
6. **Reanimated 3 for animations.** The legacy Animated API is forbidden in new code.
7. **`expo-secure-store` > `AsyncStorage`** for any sensitive data (tokens, credentials, PII).
8. **Prefer `expo-*` packages** over React Native community packages when Expo ships an equivalent.
9. **Touch targets ≥ 44pt iOS / 48dp Android.** Respect platform Human Interface Guidelines.
10. **Never hardcode API keys.** Read from `.env` via `expo-constants`. `.env.local` is gitignored; `.env.example` documents required variables.

### Install (mobile)
```powershell
pwsh -File scripts/install-shadcn-mcp.ps1 -Platform mobile -Apply
```
Or auto-detect (reads `expo` in package.json):
```powershell
pwsh -File scripts/install-shadcn-mcp.ps1 -Apply
```
The script runs `npx shadcn@latest init` (which detects Expo), installs NativeWind + class-variance-authority + clsx + tailwind-merge, configures `tailwind.config.js` + `global.css`, and optionally scaffolds RNR primitives.

### Mobile CLAUDE.md template

Run `cp .cursor/templates/CLAUDE.md.mobile.md ./CLAUDE.md` (or append to the existing CLAUDE.md) when bootstrapping a mobile project. The template contains the non-negotiables above in machine-readable form so Claude Code / Cursor respect them on every generation.

