## Cross-platform track (Platform = `cross`)

When a project ships both web and mobile from the same monorepo:

- **Shared tokens:** one source in `packages/design-tokens/` or similar. Both tracks consume.
- **Shared primitives:** RNR uses `rn-primitives` on native and `radix-ui/primitives` on web — API is compatible. Most components have an 80%+ identical surface across platforms.
- **Divergent surfaces:** navigation differs (Expo Router on mobile, Next.js routing on web). Screens / pages are separate trees. Component library is shared.
- **memory/14 §Platform = `cross`:** fills BOTH Web-specific and Mobile-specific sections.
- **DESIGN.md:** single file with both tracks documented; tooling reads per context.

