## DESIGN.md (portable cross-tool export)

memory/14 is the per-project source of truth inside MASTERMIND. DESIGN.md is its **exported portable twin** in the format that Claude Design, Google Stitch, Cursor, v0, Claude Code, and others have standardized on (9 sections: Visual Theme, Color Palette & Roles, Typography, Component Stylings, Layout Principles, Depth & Elevation, Do's and Don'ts, Responsive Behavior, Agent Prompt Guide).

- **Generate / regenerate:** `pwsh -File scripts/export-design-md.ps1` (reads memory/14 + scaffolds DESIGN.md at project root).
- **Memory/14 is canonical.** DESIGN.md is derived. Never edit DESIGN.md manually; changes will be overwritten on re-export. Edit memory/14, then regenerate.
- **Share with external tools:** point Claude Design / Stitch / v0 at `DESIGN.md` and they stay on-brand.

---

## Anti-patterns (both platforms)

- **Silently copy a random shadcn/RNR block from the docs** into the codebase without the CLI. Breaks the registry record and the project-aware Skill.
- **Edit files under `src/components/ui/` without a reason captured in memory/14**. These are "yours" by copy-paste, but untracked drift kills consistency.
- **Use Claude Design without linking the repo.** Output will be beautiful generic IA aesthetic that matches no other project you own.
- **Treat memory/14 as optional.** If it's empty, agents fall back to defaults and the per-project coherence evaporates.
- **Add a second design system in parallel** (MUI + shadcn) "just for this feature". Default answer: no. If essential, log as decision.
- **Mobile-specific:** Platform.OS branches everywhere; forgetting SafeAreaView; using Animated legacy API; AsyncStorage for tokens; more than 2 font weights; modals stacked three deep.
- **Web-specific:** inline `style={{...}}` everywhere instead of Tailwind; bespoke theming when tokens would do; sticky headers on content pages; gradient soup.
